<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maulana Abul Kalam Azad Arabic Persian Research Institute</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maulana Abul Kalam Azad Arabic Persian Research Institute is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> library and research centre at Tonk in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, established by the state government in 1978. Its collection grew from the library of the Nawabs of Tonk and holds thousands of Arabic, Persian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urdu">Urdu</a> manuscripts and rare books, including illuminated Qur'ans, making it one of the major collections of Islamic manuscripts in India.</p></div>
